routes.brief:
This is the candidate proposed by PAPER-LI-LIU-22. Li–Liu, Ann. of Math. 194 (2021), 817–901, is its foundation: it proves the arithmetic inner product formula and the Chow-group nonvanishing when E/F is unramified. The sequel (PAPER-LI-LIU-22) adds ramified places and arbitrary components at split places. Plan the two papers as one Part II, with the 2021 argument as the main line and the sequel's changes as extensions of the same stages.

Import:
- UnitaryRapoportZinkSpacesAndRSZModels: the auxiliary moduli X′_L, 𝒴, the Drinfeld-level, smooth and strictly semistable models, and uniformization.
- UnitaryKudlaRapoportCycles: the integral special cycles, their K-theory classes and the local Kudla–Rapoport identities (Li–Zhang Theorems 3.4.1 and 10.5.1).
- AutomorphicPadicLFunctions L4: the doubling embedding, Siegel Eisenstein series and local doubling zeta integrals.
- MetaplecticAutomorphicForms MP.2–MP.3 and AutomorphicLFunctionsAndLocalFactors AL.0: the Weil representation and Fourier analysis.
- ModularityAndLanglandsExtensions ML.4 and AutomorphicGaloisRepresentationsPartII AG2.2, AG2.5: Arthur's multiplicity formula, base change and the Galois representations ρ_{Π_j}.
- IgusaVarietiesAndTorsionConcentration: the vanishing Lemma 7.3.
- Cohomological tools planned elsewhere: EtaleDualityAndPerverseSheaves EDC.3 (cycle classes), ArithmeticGaloisDuality R02.2 (Hochschild–Serre), WeightsInEtaleCohomology R34.5 (weights), LefschetzPencilsAndVanishingCycles LPV.7 (the weight spectral sequence), SchemeKTheoryOperations S.6–S.7 and MotivicEtaleKTheory M.8 (K-theory with supports and Chern classes), SchemeAndStackFoundations SF.2 (absolute purity).

Construct:
- the running notation of §2 (Herm_m, Hasse invariants, Diff(T, V), nearby spaces, the lattice Λ^R and the Hecke algebras T^R ⊇ S^R, the groups G_m with their measures and automorphic spaces, the subgroups CH^m(X)^{⟨ℓ⟩});
- the doubling L-function and the Siegel–Weil measure d^♮h;
- Kudla's special cycles and generating functions, conditional on the modularity Hypothesis 4.5, and the arithmetic theta lifting;
- Beilinson's ℓ-adic height pairing and its local indices: the whole of Appendix B, including the K-theoretic computation on regular models and the ℓ-tempered correspondences. Plan it as a general tool, since nothing in the atlas plans Beilinson heights for higher-codimension cycles;
- Green currents and harmonic Green currents;
- R-good primes, admissible sextuples and the normalized height pairing (Hypothesis 6.6 stays explicit).

The final theorems:
- Proposition 3.7, with C_r = (−1)^r 2^{−2r} π^{r²} Γ(1)⋯Γ(r)/(Γ(r+1)⋯Γ(2r)) as in the final version (arXiv v5 has 2^{r(r−1)}; sourceIssues E1);
- Propositions 3.10 and 3.13, with Lemmas A.1–A.2;
- Lemma 3.15 and Remark 3.16;
- Propositions 6.9 and 6.10;
- the local-index Propositions 7.1, 8.1, 9.1 and 10.1, with Lemmas 8.3 and 9.2;
- Lemma 11.1, Theorems 1.5 and 1.7, and Corollary 1.9.

Keep F ≠ Q, V^ram = ∅ (removed in the sequel) and all 2-adic places split. Keep Hypotheses 4.5 and 6.6 as explicit hypotheses.

Proposition 9.1 uses Li–Zhang Theorem 10.5.1, which is conditional on Li–Zhang Conjecture 10.4.1 (sourceIssues E3). Import it only once the UnitaryKudlaRapoportCycles design has either Li–Rapoport–Zhang (arXiv:2404.02214) Theorem 14.6.2 or the conjecture as an explicit hypothesis. Until then Theorems 1.5 and 1.7 carry that hypothesis.

Tests:
- r = 1 against Liu 2011 (U(1, 1));
- the constant C_r and ⟨φ^0, φ^0⟩ = 2^{−2r²};
- the sign (−1)^r in Corollary 1.9;
- vol(L_u) = (q + 1)/(q^{2r} − 1) against (9.2)–(9.3).

This reuses the candidate proposed by PAPER-LI-ZHANG-22-B and extended by PAPER-LI-LIU-22; keep it moduli-theoretic. Li–Liu, Ann. of Math. 194 (2021), add the following, all over O_K with K generated by E_u and the reflex field of an admissible CM type.

Construct:
- the moduli interpretation of X′_L = X_L ⊗_E Y (Lemma 5.2, following RSZ20 §3.2 and LTXZZ §4.1), with T_0 and the CM moduli Y;
- the comparison of Shimura varieties for different complex embeddings (Lemma 5.5);
- admissible CM types and the finite étale integral model 𝒴 (Notation 5.6; Howard 2012 Prop. 3.1.2);
- the Drinfeld-level models 𝒳_m at a split place (RSZ20 Thm. 4.5; regular for m > 0 because K/E_u is unramified);
- the smooth models at an inert place with self-dual level (Li–Zhang §11.2) and their uniformization (8.2) (Li–Zhang §13.1);
- the strictly semistable models at an almost self-dual inert place (Li–Zhang §11.3), with the decomposition of the special fibre into Y° (a P^{2r−1}-fibration), Y• (proper smooth) and Y† (a relative Fermat hypersurface) (LTXZZ §§5.1–5.5).

The almost self-dual models need p unramified in E and u unramified over Q (footnote 18). LTXZZ's extra conditions on u are asserted removable (footnote 19); check this before relying on it.

Tests:
- 𝒳_0 smooth and 𝒳_m ⊗ K ≅ X′_{L_{u,m}L^u} ⊗ K;
- the two components of the special fibre and their intersection in rank n = 2.

This reuses the candidate proposed by PAPER-LI-ZHANG-22-B. Li–Liu 2021 consume its global special cycles and its two local identities. Add:
- the moduli description of special cycles on X′_L, finite and unramified over it (Definition 5.3, Lemma 5.4);
- the integral special cycles 𝒵_T(φ^∞)_L on the smooth and semistable models (Li–Zhang §13.3), their K-theory classes in F^r K^Z_0 (Gillet–Soulé Prop. 5.5) and their uniformization (8.3);
- the classes ^K𝒩(x) (Zhang 2021 App. B);
- the Euler-characteristic identities χ(π^∧_*{}^K𝒩(x)) at self-dual level (Li–Zhang Thm. 3.4.1, Rem. 3.4.2) and at almost self-dual level (Li–Zhang Thm. 10.5.1, Rem. 10.5.4), exported in the Whittaker normalization used here.

The almost self-dual identity is conditional in Li–Zhang on their Conjecture 10.4.1 (Kudla–Rapoport). Either import Li–Rapoport–Zhang arXiv:2404.02214 Theorem 14.6.2, after checking that it supplies parts (i)–(iii) of that conjecture, or keep the conjecture as a named hypothesis (sourceIssues E3).
